# Execution Environment

This project uses pyenv. Before running Python, pip, or project scripts in the shell, initialize pyenv:

```bash
export PYENV_ROOT="$HOME/.pyenv"
export PATH="$PYENV_ROOT/bin:$PATH"
pyenv init - | source /dev/stdin
```

Then run commands from the project root so `.python-version` (3.13.13) is picked up.

Example:

```bash
export PYENV_ROOT="$HOME/.pyenv"
export PATH="$PYENV_ROOT/bin:$PATH"
pyenv init - | source /dev/stdin
cd /data/home/arul/dev/thedal
python search_jobs.py profiles/data-engineer.example.json
```

Do not use the system Python at `/apps/linux-rhel8/python/venv-3.8.16/bin/python3` for this project.
